    "«Calm time» is the share of the last month that sat in the Low band; «steadiness» is how much your daily index varies week to week (its coefficient of variation: lower is steadier). The Low / Moderate / High bands (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) are the same for everyone because the index is already adjusted to your own baseline. (Plews 2013)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Calm time» is the share of the last month that sat in the Low band; «steadiness» is how much your daily index varies week to week (its coefficient of variation: lower is steadier). The Low / Moderate / High bands (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) are the same for everyone because the index is already adjusted to your own baseline. (Plews 2013)"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "«Tiempo en calma» es la parte del último mes que cayó en la banda Baja; «regularidad» es cuánto varía tu índice día a día de semana a semana (su coeficiente de variación: menor es más estable). Las bandas Baja / Moderada / Alta (0–1 / 1–2 / 2–3) son iguales para todos porque el índice ya está ajustado a tu propia base. (Plews 2013)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
