          }
        }
      }
    },
    "We need a few more nights to show your 7-day average, your normal range and the trend." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "We need a few more nights to show your 7-day average, your normal range and the trend."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Necesitamos unas noches más para mostrar tu media de 7 días, tu rango normal y la tendencia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "We need a few more nights of sleep to learn your baseline before we score your recovery. We'd rather not show a made-up number." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "We need a few more nights of sleep to learn your baseline before we score your recovery. We'd rather not show a made-up number."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Necesitamos algunas noches más de sueño para aprender tu línea base antes de calificar tu recuperación. Preferimos no mostrar un número inventado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "We need about 6 sessions of the same sport to start showing how you wake afterward. Keep logging your workouts and this fills in on its own." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "We need about 6 sessions of the same sport to start showing how you wake afterward. Keep logging your workouts and this fills in on its own."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Necesitamos unas 6 sesiones de un mismo deporte para empezar a ver cómo amaneces después. Sigue registrando tus entrenamientos y esto se llena solo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The number you see is the HRV Apple records overnight: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. The read that tells you how recovered you are uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights. RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-digest branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches of your nervous system; that, plus the two being measured over different nightly windows, means the HRV number here won't always line up with the direction of your recovery." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The number you see is the HRV Apple records overnight: SDNN, the overall spread of the time between your heartbeats. The read that tells you how recovered you are uses a different HRV measure, RMSSD, recomputed from the beat-to-beat intervals of your densest nights. RMSSD tracks the vagal, rest-and-digest branch specifically, while SDNN blends both branches of your nervous system; that, plus the two being measured over different nightly windows, means the HRV number here won't always line up with the direction of your recovery."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "El número que ves es el HRV que Apple registra de noche: SDNN, la dispersión general del tiempo entre tus latidos. Tu lectura de recuperación usa otra medida de HRV —RMSSD— recalculada de los intervalos latido a latido de tus noches más densas. El RMSSD sigue específicamente la rama vagal (de descanso), mientras que el SDNN mezcla ambas ramas de tu sistema nervioso; eso, sumado a que se calculan sobre ventanas distintas de la noche, hace que el número de HRV de aquí no siempre coincida con la dirección de tu recuperación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "We take today's resting heart rate and HRV and express each as how far it sits from your 30-day average (a z-score). A resting HR above your norm and an HRV below it both add to the load; the two are summed and squashed onto a 0–3 scale where 0 is calm, 1.5 is your baseline, and 3 is highly activated." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "We take today's resting heart rate and HRV and express each as how far it sits from your 30-day average (a z-score). A resting HR above your norm and an HRV below it both add to the load; the two are summed and squashed onto a 0–3 scale where 0 is calm, 1.5 is your baseline, and 3 is highly activated."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Tomamos tu frecuencia cardíaca en reposo y tu HRV de hoy y expresamos cada una como qué tan lejos está de tu promedio de 30 días (un z-score). Una FC en reposo por arriba de tu norma y una HRV por debajo suman a la carga; las dos se combinan y se ajustan a una escala de 0 a 3, donde 0 es calma, 1.5 es tu línea base y 3 es muy activado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
